<!--
doc/src/sgml/ref/cypher_merge.sgml
PostgreSQL documentation
-->

<refentry id="cypher-merge">
 <indexterm zone="cypher-merge">
  <primary>CYPHER MERGE</primary>
 </indexterm>

 <refmeta>
  <refentrytitle>CYPHER MERGE</refentrytitle>
  <manvolnum>7</manvolnum>
  <refmiscinfo>SQL - Language Statements</refmiscinfo>
 </refmeta>

 <refnamediv>
  <refname>CYPHER MERGE</refname>
  <refpurpose>merge the cypher elements to target</refpurpose>
 </refnamediv>

 <refsynopsisdiv>
<synopsis>

MERGE <literal>path_pattern</literal>
    [ { ON CREATE SET | ON MATCH SET } <replaceable class="parameter">cypher_expr</replaceable> = <replaceable class="parameter">cypher_expr</replaceable> ]

<literal>path_pattern</literal> can be one of:

    <literal>node_pattern</literal>
    <literal>path_pattern</literal> <literal>edge_pattern</literal> <literal>node_pattern</literal>
    <replaceable class="parameter">path_variable_name</replaceable> = <literal>path_pattern</literal>

and <literal>node_pattern</literal> is:

    ( [<replaceable class="parameter">variable_name</replaceable>][<replaceable class="parameter">:label_name</replaceable>] [ ONLY ] [ <literal>cypher_property_map</literal> ] )

and <literal>edge_pattern</literal> is:

    { - | &lt;- } [ [<replaceable class="parameter">variable_name</replaceable>][<replaceable class="parameter">:label_name</replaceable>] [ONLY] [ <literal>cypher_range_pattern</literal> ] [ <literal>cypher_property_map</literal> ] ] { - | -&gt; }

and <literal>cypher_property_map</literal> is:

    { <replaceable class="parameter">property_name</replaceable> : <replaceable class="parameter">property_value</replaceable>, [ ...] }

</synopsis>
 </refsynopsisdiv>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Description</title>

  <para>
   The <command>MERGE</command> clause is a clause that 
     <orderedlist>
       <listitem><para>If the specified pattern does not exist in the graph, adds a corresponding pattern (like the CREATE clause)</para></listitem>
       <listitem><para>If it already exists in the graph, verifies existence of the pattern (like the Match clause).</para></listitem>
     </orderedlist>
   The MERGE clause recognizes the entire pattern specified in the clause.
  </para>

 </refsect1>

 <refsect1>
  <title>Parameters</title>

   <variablelist>

    <varlistentry>
     <term><literal>ON CREATE SET</literal></term>
     <listitem>
      <para>
       The <literal>ON CREATE SET</literal> clauses can be used to set properties depending
       on how the MERGE clause behaves. If the MERGE clause behaves like a CREATE clause,
       the ON CREATE SET clause will be performed;
      </para>
     </listitem>
    </varlistentry>

    <varlistentry>
     <term><literal>ON MATCH SET</literal></term>
     <listitem>
      <para>
       The <literal>ON CREATE SET</literal> clauses can be used to set properties depending
       on how the MERGE clause behaves. If the MERGE clause behaves like a MATCH clause,
       the ON MATCH SET clause will be performed;
      </para>
     </listitem>
    </varlistentry>

   </variablelist>

  <refsect2>
   <title><replaceable class="parameter">path_pattern</replaceable></title>
   <para>
    Mainly, represent about the cypher path expression.
    See <xref linkend="cypher-path-pattern"/> for more examples.
   </para>
  </refsect2>

  <refsect2>
   <title><literal>cypher_expr</literal></title>
   <para>
    Basic expression of the cypher query.
    See <xref linkend="cypher-expr"/> for more examples.
   </para>
  </refsect2>

 </refsect1>


 <refsect1>
  <title>Examples</title>

  <para>
   To merge a vertex:
<programlisting>
MERGE (:person {name: 'Edward'});
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   To merge a path:
<programlisting>
MERGE (E:person {name: 'Edward'})-[L:likes]->(A:person {name: 'Alice'})
RETURN E, L, A;
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   To merge a path but step by step merge:
<programlisting>
MERGE (E:person {name: 'Edward'})
MERGE (A:person {name: 'Alice'})
MERGE (E)-[L:likes]->(A)
RETURN E, L, A;
</programlisting>
  </para>

  <para>
   To merge a vertex with <literal>ON CREATE SET</literal> and <literal>ON MATCH SET</literal>:
<programlisting>
-- Vertex will be newly merged:
MERGE (E:person {name: 'Edward'})
ON CREATE SET E.lastop = 'CREATE'
ON MATCH SET E.lastop = 'MATCH'
RETURN E.lastop;
  lastop  
----------
 "CREATE"
(1 row)

-- Do the same query again:
MERGE (E:person {name: 'Edward'})
ON CREATE SET E.lastop = 'CREATE'
ON MATCH SET E.lastop = 'MATCH'
RETURN E.lastop;
  lastop  
----------
 "MATCH"
(1 row)
</programlisting>
  </para>

 </refsect1>


  <refsect1>
  <title>See Also</title>

  <simplelist type="inline">
   <member><xref linkend="cypher-match"/></member>
   <member><xref linkend="cypher-create"/></member>
  </simplelist>
 </refsect1>
</refentry>



